WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.736
-Today is my final day
before a haircut

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.870
and our last show
in our Captain's quarters

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.540
and it's bittersweet
because there's so much,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.042
so much, we didn't get to.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.777
For example,
I had hoped to introduce

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.479
a talking Jon Hamm painting
that didn't wanna be here.

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:15.281
-I don't like this bit.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.683
I don't wanna do it.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.451
-I wanted to do a bit
about checking in

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.620
with my friend Ethan Hawke,
who I'd put in charge

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.922
of exterminating the wasps
in my attic.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.958
-Seth, th-they've
taken over, man!

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.861
They've learned how
to use tools!

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:31.397
It's a --
It's a [bleep] nightmare!

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.233
-And I wanted Amy Schumer
to be my first, and only,

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.802
Captain's quarters
in-studio guest.

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:37.937 line:0%
-You ran out of time?

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.039 line:0%
-I thought your people
would've told you.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.109
-No. I've been sitting here
for an hour and a half.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.377
I-I --

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.645
-Oh, I --
-Can I just plug --

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:46.946
Can I plug my show really quick?

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.581
-We really are short on time.
-Okay. Should I go?

00:00:49.581 --> 00:00:50.916
-That'd be great.
Thank you, Amy.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:53.553 line:0%
And thank -- I'm so sorry.
This is awful.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.621 line:0%
-Okay.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.723 line:0%
-And I just need you to, um,

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.458 line:0%
just keep 15 feet.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.826 line:0%
-15?
-Yeah.

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.260 line:0%
-I think it's six.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.729 line:0%
-I think you can make it
right over top of that thing.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:04.863 line:0%
Thank you, Amy.
-Well, thank you.

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:05.865 line:0%
-I'm so sorry about this.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.933 line:0%
-Me too.
I really wish I'd known.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:10.336 line:0%
I took a ferry, you know.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:11.804 line:0%
I took a ferry here.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:13.105 line:0%
-You -- Oh.
-I was told I could promote

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:15.174 line:0%
my -- my show.
-Boy, oh, boy.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.077 line:0%
-"Inside Amy Schumer"?
-No!

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.012 line:0%
-Oh.
-The cooking show!

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:22.215 line:0%
And just --
but maybe in the city,

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.517 line:0%
I could talk about my show?
-That'd be great.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.285
We just didn't have the time.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:28.387
It's also the last day
with all our friends behind me

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.089
and I'm happy to report
that everyone who went

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.557
on this journey with us

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:32.926
found what they were
looking for.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.461
-I got a new voice!
-I got cleaned.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:36.963
-Yeah, I got my own podcast

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.232
and, if you could tweet
about it or whatnot,

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.034
my people think that
could be very helpful.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.368
-And it turned out
the ghost lobster

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.869
who long tormented
the Sea Captain

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.405
only wanted companionship
and, once he discovered that,

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.841
the Sea Captain
not only forgave him,

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.844
he offered him the job
of first mate on his ship.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.946
-Thank you, Sea Captain.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:55.915
-Thank you, friend.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.917
-And the Sea Captain, well,

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.086
he maybe got
the best gift of all.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:03.256
-I got to participate
in a long, psychotic bit

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:07.426
that would have eaten [bleep]
in front of a live audience.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.862
-Speaking of psychos...
-Final summer segue!

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.164
-...yet another of the
president's close confidantes,

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:14.300
his former campaign manager
and chief strategist,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.501
was arrested today

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.204
for a wild scam
that captures so much

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.472
of what's rotten about Trumpism.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.741
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:25.477
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:27.313
I don't need to tell you guys
that everything's bad

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.748
and good news is very rare,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:32.018
but when it does come along,
why not gorge ourselves on it?

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.186
Even when it comes later
in the day,

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:35.021
causing you to rip up
a finished "Closer Look"

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.222
and start from scratch.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.623
Hey, you guys remember
Steve Bannon,

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.425
the white nationalist/
giant pimple

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.661
who ran Trump's campaign;
then worked in his White House

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:45.264
and helped engineers such odious
policies as the Muslim ban

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.632
and who publicly defended

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.368
the horrific
family separation policy;

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.704
often wore two shirts,
when one would've sufficed?

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.072
You know, the dude who had

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.441
a crazy-person whiteboard
in his office,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.943
with policies scrawled on it,

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.946
like "Suspend immigration
from terror-prone regions,

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.981
Implement new extreme
vetting techniques,

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.683
and Suspend the
Syrian Refugee Program."

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:05.852
I'm shocked it didn't
also include

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.754
"Brunch with Slenderman"
and "kill the Batman."

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.089
You know, Steve Bannon,

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.624
the gentleman
who currently looks

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.426
like a guy selling
exotic reptiles

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.060
on the Venice Beach Boardwalk.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.495
Steve Bannon wasn't born.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.965
He just burst out of someone's
chest, Quatto-style.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.933
He looks like
a "Where are you now"

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:24.170
about the face-melt skeleton
from "Raiders of the Lost Ark."

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.871
Look at this.
It's like if the Cryptkeeper

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:27.373
spent a month
in a tanning booth.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.677
Well, now that we've piled on,
we can move on.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.046
Oh! Wait. I forgot.
One more thing.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.847
You guys,
[ Laughing ] he got arrested.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.982
-News just coming out from the
Southern District of New York,

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:39.184 line:0%
saying Steve Bannon
and three other men

00:03:39.184 --> 00:03:42.487 line:0%
have been arrested
and indicted and charged,

00:03:42.487 --> 00:03:44.356 line:0%
in relation to their role

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:46.692 line:0%
in a nonprofit organization
called We Build the Wall.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:50.663 line:0%
It's a crowdfunding organization
that, the FDNY says,

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:56.235 line:0%
has raised about $25 million
for wall-related funding.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:59.271 line:0%
What the indictment here
is alleging

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.639 line:0%
is that Bannon and his others

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:03.676 line:0%
were skimming some
of the proceeds

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.312 line:0%
from that fundraising
for themselves,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.948 line:0%
even though they had
suggested publicly

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.617 line:0%
that this was a volunteer
organization

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.152 line:0%
and they were not
taking salaries.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.721 line:0%
-Steve Bannon, through
a nonprofit organization

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:17.923 line:0%
under his control --
nonprofit one,

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:19.992 line:0%
as it's referred to here
in the document --

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.694 line:0%
received over $1 million
from We Build the Wall,

00:04:22.694 --> 00:04:24.497 line:0%
at least some of which,
they say,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.833 line:0%
Bannon used to cover hundreds
of thousands of dollars

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:30.402 line:0%
in his own personal expenses.

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:32.438
-You know what, baby?
It's been a brutal six months,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.240
so I'm gonna mainline
some schadenfreude.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.375
Line that up on a mirror

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.043
and give me a dollar bill
to snort it with.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.911 line:0%
[ Snorts ]
Whoo!

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.846
Seriously, did prosecutors know

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.948
this was our last summer show
in the Captain's quarters?

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:45.618
Because this is
a fantastic parting gift.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.486
That's right,
Steve Bannon was arrested

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:50.523
for allegedly skimming
$1 million from a scam charity

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.591
that claimed to be raising money

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.225
to build
the Southern border wall.

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:56.562
This is the perfect
encapsulation of the Trump era.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.198
From beginning to end,
the wall was a nonstop scam.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.333
Trump scammed his supporters

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.402
by telling them Mexico
would pay for it.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.836
Then, we ended up paying for it.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.572
Then, this baked-potato
Fabio over here

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.673
said he'd raise money for it.

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.375
Then, he scammed everyone again

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.410
by allegedly skimming
money from it.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.845
It's a Russian nesting doll
of fraud.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.882
I can't wait until Bannon raises
money for his legal defense fund

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.717
and we find out he lost it
all at the racetrack.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.986
"Sir, please,
we'd love you to leave.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.220
You're scaring the horses."

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.322
And, as NBC's Pete Williams
reported today,

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:26.525
it's pretty obvious this thing
was a scam from the jump.

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.127
-According
to the court documents,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:32.731
this We Build the Wall thing
came and flamed out quickly.

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:35.267 line:0%
According
to the court documents,

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:39.806 line:0%
the founder of it,
this man, Brian Kolfage,

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:42.508 line:0%
said that he would not take
any of the money,

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.710 line:0%
that it was entirely
a volunteer effort,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.445 line:0%
but it's said he did take
a lot of money.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.582 line:0%
And, as for Steve Bannon,
it says

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:54.053 line:0%
he formed a nonprofit
organization that he controlled.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:58.558 line:0%
It received about $1 million
from this crowdfunding effort,

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.760 line:0%
some of which,
the Justice Department says,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.062 line:0%
he used to cover --
and I'm quoting here now --

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.063 line:0%
"hundreds of thousands
of dollars

00:06:05.063 --> 00:06:07.232 line:0%
in Bannon's personal expenses."

00:06:07.232 --> 00:06:09.101 line:0%
The court documents
basically say

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:11.937 line:0%
that this thing
was pretty suspect

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:14.073 line:0%
almost from the beginning.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.607
-I mean, of course it was.

00:06:15.607 --> 00:06:16.975
A crowdsourced fundraiser

00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:18.944
to build a [bleep] wall
in the middle of the desert?

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:21.514
The only way it could've been
a more obvious scam is

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:24.416
if they offered free boner pills
with every donation.

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:27.353
The thing was one rung
below those companies

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.421
that claim to name
a star after you.

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:32.924
"Oh, yeah, that one up there
is -- that's, uh, Dan.

00:06:32.924 --> 00:06:33.960
That will be 5,000 bucks.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.094
Cash only."

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.295
The details of this arrest

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.596
are just absolutely incredible.

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:39.732
Every little tidbit
is better than the last.

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.735
For example, according to CNN,
Bannon was arrested

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:45.137
on a boat Thursday off the
eastern coast of Connecticut

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:46.939 line:0%
by federal agents,
along with officials

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.441 line:0%
from the United States
Postal Inspection Service.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:52.711
He got arrested on a boat
by the postal service.

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:54.847
The postal service has a navy?!

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:57.649
Please tell me it's just a mail
truck with a giant cannon.

00:06:57.649 --> 00:06:59.818
Nothin' is more fun
than imagining

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:01.420
a bunch of postal service
inspectors,

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.521
in their short shorts,

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:04.523
boarding a yacht
and arresting Steve Bannon

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:06.558
in a dramatic
high seas sting operation,

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:08.027
swingin' down on a rope,

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:09.662
carrying letter openers
like swords.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.664
How has there never been
a "CSI: Post Office"?

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:14.266
Something tells me David Caruso

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:15.801
would definitely
come back for that.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.737
[ As Caine ]
Looks like this package
has been

00:07:18.737 --> 00:07:19.939
returned to sender.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.774
-♪ Yeah! ♪

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.175
-That's how he held
his hands, right,

00:07:23.175 --> 00:07:26.078
after he put on his glasses,
very delicately, like this?

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:27.346
Like he was still holdin' 'em.

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:28.814
Seriously, think
about how perfect this is.

00:07:28.814 --> 00:07:31.450
The same public agency Trump is
currently trying to destroy,

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.819
one of the most cherished
public institutions in America,

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:35.721
arrested his former
campaign manager

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:38.690
for allegedly skimming money
from a fundraiser

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.893
for their scam border wall,
two days after we found out

00:07:41.893 --> 00:07:43.329
Trump's previous
campaign manager

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.064
colluded with Russian
intelligence.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.865
It's like the end
of the summer TV season

00:07:46.865 --> 00:07:48.867
and they're wrappin' up
all the story arcs at once.

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:51.637 line:0%
This really is such a perfect
encapsulation of Trumpism.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:52.838 line:0%
It's all a giant grift.

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:54.473 line:0%
Bannon was gettin' rich,
and so was Trump.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.141 line:0%
The dude's constantly
at his own properties.

00:07:56.141 --> 00:07:57.376 line:0%
Lobbyists and foreign officials

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:58.811 line:0%
